WEBVTT

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.980
Damn it... They keep coming, 
one after another.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.420
They don't give up.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.260
<i>The two of us came all the way to Mars</i>

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.730
<i>just to be trapped by an army of terraformars.</i>

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.330
The Special Two

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.280
<i>Talk about a life or death situation.</i>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.590
Should you be laughing 
right now, Michelle-san?

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.970
It's because you're watching my back.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:41.770
Huh?

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.920
Akari, you can keep going, right?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.920
Yes...

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.820
We made that promise, after all.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.080
Promise?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:01.080
If we beat these guys, I get 
to see your shower scene.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.070
I never made that promise!

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.730
It's against the rules, 
but it can't be helped.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.920
But I'm sure we'll be able to make it work.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.670
Let's finish this in one shot.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:15.630
Right!

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.980
<i>In the year 2020,</i>

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.300
<i>cockroaches were sent to Mars along with moss,</i>

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.100
<i>which would be their food source,</i>

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.070
<i>as part of a terraforming plan to make Mars 
habitable and relieve Earth's overpopulation.</i>

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:03.180
<i>However, 600 years later, that would 
provide humanity two nightmares...</i>

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:08.060
<i>The cockroaches underwent an 
unexpected evolution on Mars,</i>

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.300
<i>becoming creatures known as "terraformars,"</i>

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.360
<i>and a communicable disease called the 
Alien Engine Virus, which originated on Mars</i>

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.110
<i>and has a 100% fatality rate in humans, 
is currently plaguing Earth.</i>

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.550
<i>In order to capture the 
1,000 terraformar samples</i>

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:24.160
<i>needed to create a vaccine, 
many young people</i>

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.690
<i>underwent a special surgical procedure</i>

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.460
<i>and were sent off to Mars.</i>

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.590
<b>Evil Planet</b>

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:48.720
<i>On this distant, evil planet, will humanity 
be able to obtain their hope for tomorrow?</i>

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.160
<i>Can you all hear me?</i>

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.180
Captain!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.260
I want to confirm the status 
of No. 1 and No. 2 Divisions.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.040
Report your status!

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.380
All members of No. 2 Division are safe.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.130
We're holding back the west side.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.540
Having to stay up late 
because of these guys...

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.220
You can't be serious!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.220
<b>My skin's going to
get damaged!</b>

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.270
My skin's going to get damaged!

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.180
This is No. 1 Division.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:55.810
All the civilians are in the escape vessel, but...

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.480
Th-They're nearby!

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.400
<i>What?!</i>

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.810
<i>No. 1 Division, I can't say we're 
in an ideal situation, either.</i>

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.070
<i>We'll head over as soon we're done here.</i>

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.860
<i>Do what you can to survive.</i>

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:14.040
No... I'm going to protect the 
medicine, no matter what.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.250
<i>Escape vessel, just a little longer!</i>

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.420
As soon as I take care of the 
wounded, I'll head over!

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.320
Michelle, are you okay over there?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.800
<i>Yeah... For the record, 
both of us have injected twice.</i>

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:25.420
What?!

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.130
<i>Hey, it's too soon!</i>

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.650
It's better than becoming their food!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.360
<i>Hizamaru Akari.</i>

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.310
<i>You've gone way past your limit.</i>

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.610
<i>And yet, this passion...</i>

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.240
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.750
<i>That girl who was more than your friend, 
but not quite your girlfriend,</i>

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.700
<i>is already gone.</i>

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.660
<i>Yes...</i>

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.050
<i>We made that promise, after all.</i>

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.880
<i>I see...</i>

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.840
Hey, can I fix that?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.810
I'm really good at that stuff.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.790
You are?

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.820
I've been over there, 
but haven't had anything to do.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.280
<i>The AE virus...</i>

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.730
I'm Harukaze Sakurato.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.960
<i>The boy inflicted with the AE virus...</i>

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.870
<i>We made that promise, after all.</i>

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.870
Did you come to say goodbye?

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.500
He'll be quarantined soon, too.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.890
Don't say anything that'll give him hope.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.200
The mission to Mars is cruel.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.030
Even if we're able to get the samples,

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:01.980
there's no proof that the 
vaccine will be made in time.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.670
I know.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.240
Here.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:12.070
Wow, not bad, kid.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.610
Thanks.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.470
Hey.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.040
Is it true that you're going to Mars?

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.000
Yeah.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:24.000
So we probably won't see each other again.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.440
Why would you say that?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.460
Because...

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:34.470
We're going to Mars to find 
a cure for your sickness.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:35.660
Really?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:38.720
It might be a very small, distant hope,

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.390
but wait for us, and don't give up.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:42.480
I'll leave that with you.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.520
So I can wait for you?

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.800
Leave it to me!

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.050
You fool.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.810
<i>Promise, eh?</i>

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.380
<i>Damn...</i>

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.320
<i>What are you? The hero 
of some shonen manga?</i>

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.540
<i>The second dose definitely takes its toll...</i>

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.380
Akari, are you all right? 
We're heading to No. 1 Division's ship.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.850
Akari!

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.160
<i>Like hell I'm going to lose!</i>

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.520
The net! The net!

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.000
Hurry, everyone!

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.590
You idiot! What are you doing?!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:51.630
Well...

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.380
Yaeko!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.250
<i>Dawn?</i>

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:19.070
Are you planning to crash us into the ground?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.530
Alex!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.140
Don't you dare underestimate

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:05.420
the grip strength of a (future) 
major league pitcher!

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:07.160
Alex!

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.850
Captain!

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.570
I've regrouped with No. 1 Division.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:27.680
I've secured survivors of the crew.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:30.090
<i>Michelle, how are you doing over there?</i>

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.980
Akari was taken by those things.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.110
<i>What?!</i>

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.970
He doesn't have any medicine left.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:37.130
<i>That's not good.</i>

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.880
<i>Akari, you understand, don't you?</i>

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:42.910
<i>You and I can't fall into their hands.</i>

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.870
<i>We're both special like that.</i>

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.200
<i>So...</i>

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.220
<i>No... That's not it.</i>

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:53.060
<i>Anyway, just don't die, Akari!</i>

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:59.500
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.110
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:06.310
<i>That's right... Mars.</i>

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.450
<i>I... I...</i>

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.270
Sakurato.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:17.520
Is there anything you want 
to eat when you get better?

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:20.740
French fries!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.070
All right! I'll buy you a large order of fries!

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:23.980
Really?!

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.550
But my mom says I can't even have a small...

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:28.720
I'll even get you a double L or a triple L!

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:30.750
Those don't exist.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:32.580
<i>Akari...</i>

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.880
<i>Is that your only promise?</i>

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:37.880
What else?

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.790
I wanna do karate.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.710
Oh, sounds good.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:52.970
I wanna go to the ocean, too.

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:53.650
Sure!

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.220
<i>You...</i>

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:06.370
And the zoo!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.400
Yeah!

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.090
And then... And then...

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.900
<i>The girl who had the same virus as him...</i>

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:13.950
I want to eat ramen.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:22.180
All right! I'll find a great place!

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:23.510
I want to go snowboarding.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.800
Then I'll buy the gear.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.570
I want to try alcohol.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:28.820
Sure. Just don't drink too much.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.670
If I fall asleep, give me a piggyback ride.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.270
You're so hopeless, Yuriko-chan.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.330
I want to go to Space Land, too.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:43.720
That place is enough?

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:46.120
It's probably pretty deserted.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.140
And then... And then...

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.200
And then...

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.580
Don't worry.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.580
Yeah...

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.360
We found someone to do the surgery.

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:57.540
I'll make money, and cure you.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.610
Yeah...

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.510
You'll be back to yourself in no time!

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.080
Yeah...

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:08.160
Why? Why are you so kind, Akari-kun?

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:13.240
Of course I am.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.360
<i>I'm...</i>

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:29.440
<i>We'll always be together.</i>

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.330
<i>This time, I'll...</i>

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.650
<i>We'll always be together.</i>

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:04.190
What is this sensation?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:21.840
Akari!

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:28.800
Akari!

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.130
Michelle!

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.320
Akari!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.630
I wanna do karate!

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:41.700
Akari... Sheesh, you really are something...

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.260
Ah... Michelle-san.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:49.470
Sorry.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.790
I've got nothing left.

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.430
You say that, but what's your hand doing?

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.880
Well, whatever.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:02.940
You're okay with that?

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:10.410
<i>Michelle K. Davis and Hizamaru Akari, 
the ones called the first and second.</i>

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:14.970
<i>Their story is only just beginning.</i>

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.300
No. 1 Division is all here.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.230
No. 2 Division is also all here...

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:24.380
Except one member who's out due to injury.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.930
Kouno Kaiki, and

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:28.310
Sheila Levitt...

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.730
Those eleven fought bravely, and have now

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.570
made this far-off planet 
their final resting place.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:39.140
We survivors will take 
their souls back to Earth.

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:40.830
No matter what.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:44.690
A moment of silence for those eleven souls.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:51.320
This is indeed much more of an 
emergency than we had ever imagined.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:56.390
After entering the atmosphere, 
they invaded and destroyed the main engine.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:59.100
We had no choice but to execute Plan Delta,

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:02.790
and split up into six escape vessels 
to land separately on Mars.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.710
What awaited us was a grand 
welcome from the state.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:09.930
It appears the other divisions were
probably also attacked, as well.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.170
The only one that replied was No. 5 Division.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.860
They said that No. 4 Division was annihilated.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:18.320
Other than that, No. 6 Division 
sent out an SOS once...

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.430
I haven't heard anything 
from the other divisions.

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:25.770
You're kidding... All of them, that easily?

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.240
Um, I'm sure they're all fine.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:33.250
We'll see them at the rendezvous point.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:36.990
It's just coincidence that 
we haven't heard from them.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:40.140
We got plenty of the samples we came for,

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:44.110
so let's all cheer up, 
and head toward Annex 1!

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:47.960
Huh? Did I say something wrong?

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:50.690
No, you're completely right, Yaeko.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:53.890
Let's hold on to hope and
 head back to the main ship.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.360
The path there,

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:58.220
with our vessel that can't fly 
anymore, will take about a week.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:59.720
A week?

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.640
There's not much medicine left.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.230
And so, we're gonna sleep!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:06.810
What?!

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:10.250
What's with that response? Were you 
planning to not sleep for a week?

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.470
No, but...

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:14.940
It's fine. You guys are alive, so eat and sleep.

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.180
It's true that we're worried about the

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:19.580
other divisions, and we can't 
forget about comrades who died...

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:21.160
This is a battlefield.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.500
But you guys are human.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.680
You cry when you're sad, 
scream when you're angry...

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:29.850
And when you're done with that, 
tell a joke and laugh.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:30.640
<i>She's completely different from 
when I first met her at 21.</i>

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:32.860
Otherwise, this won't be a 
battle for humanity anymore.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.710
<i>Maybe she changed because she's 
got people under her now.</i>

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.620
<i>Or maybe it's because of her comrades...</i>

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:40.550
<i>I won't mention that what you said was 
borrowed from my own speech, Michelle-chan.</i>

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.990
All right. Girls who want 
to shower, follow me.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.350
Be careful!

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.720
Yeah. Kanako, bring some 
medicine just in case.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:49.760
'Kay!

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:56.260
So good!

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:07.450
Hey! Hey!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.490
Don't get any weird ideas.

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:15.300
She can hear a killer whale's sonar, 
her ears are so good.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:21.010
Damn. I know it can't be helped, 
but this low water pressure...

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:23.970
I hope Eva-chan and the others are safe.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.190
Um... Was she in Division No. 5?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:29.020
Yeah. And she's promised to tell me something.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.240
How to make your boobs bigger.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.340
<b>Eva</b>

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:38.320
I-It'll be fine. No. 5 Division also has Adolf-san.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.310
In the meantime, I'll massage them for you.

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:41.780
Hey! Stop!

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.910
Well done.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:54.730
You have my praise.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.650
Michelle-san...

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:05.370
How are you feeling?

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.980
I'm fine.

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:09.990
I see.

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:11.730
Were you by my side this whole time?

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.630
Of course not, you fool.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.730
Right.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:17.610
Anyway, we've acquired the necessary samples.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:19.690
Now we just have to make it back to Earth.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.040
You'll be able to keep your promise.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:27.040
Really?! I get a shower scene?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.230
I already 
took one

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:34.290
I guess you're fine, if you 
can say something like that.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.370
Hey, it's the fainter.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:41.020
Amazing. Stupid people really do heal fast.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:42.970
What? You think you can say whatever you want?

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:46.530
I mean, that ball that you threw hit me!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.400
So that's what it means to be wildly popular...

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:47.400
Just like I planned.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:47.890
Why, you...

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.890
This turned into a rough night.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:56.860
I didn't want everyone to die...

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:58.390
Including No. 4 Division...

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.580
Yeah...

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.290
There's something that's been on my mind.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.320
What?

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.240
Last night, right before we regrouped,

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.780
I saw a strange light in the 
direction of No. 5 Division.

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:10.670
Adolf and the others...

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:12.660
This is a cruel analysis,

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:16.790
but Adolf, who was ranked second and 
had radar abilities, is a huge loss.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.790
Who knows when they'll attack again—

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.680
Right now, all we can do is believe

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.800
that everyone is safe.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.910
The second morning...

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:38.000
But why is it? They're not coming...

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:42.790
Now, then... It appears that 
Plan Delta has occurred.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:47.030
You've already sent a giant rescue ship, right?

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:45.930
U-NASA 5th Branch Office
German Prime Minister Petra Eheim

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:52.700
Yes, thanks to all of your support, 
as well as the people of Earth.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.430
U-NASA 6th Branch Office
Roman Commonwealth President
 Luke Snorresson

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:52.890
U-NASA 3rd Branch Office
Russian Commonwealth President Smiles

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:57.460
We've let one country carry all of the burden,

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.700
U-NASA 2nd Branch Office
Japanese Prime Minister Hiruma Ichiro

00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:58.740
U-NASA 4th Branch Office
Head

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.340
but this is in order to save humanity.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:05.360
My country believes that we should all 
provide all the strength we have together.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:03.190
U-NASA 1st Branch Office
US President Gerald Goodman

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:42.600
Michelle-san, I'm going to go 
back to Earth, no matter what.

00:22:42.950 --> 00:22:44.110
Your face is too close.

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:44.930
Huh?

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:46.960
You're tickling my ear.

00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:48.790
I'm sorry.

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:50.840
Akari, what's wrong?

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:52.550
Did she reject you?

00:23:03.890 --> 00:23:08.610
Everyone, as soon as we get back to 
Annex 1, we'll be able to see the others.

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:12.050
Let's all go back to Earth! Go, go!

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
The Enraged Captain

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:40.230
After being beaten this thoroughly... I...
